│ ┃        Patch for Template Tag Keyword Argument Handling        ┃ │
│ ┗━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┛ │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue arises from incorrect error handling when multiple       │
│ keyword arguments are provided to a template tag. The current      │
│ implementation raises a TemplateSyntaxError for overlapping        │
│ keyword arguments, but the intended behavior is to allow overrides │
│ of keyword-only arguments with defaults.                           │
│                                                                    │
│ [file]templatetags/custom_tags.py[/file] [original]                │
│ @register.simple_tag def hello(, greeting='hello'): return         │
│ f'{greeting} world' [/original] [patched] @register.simple_tag def │
│ hello(, greeting='hello'): # Check if 'greeting' is a keyword-only │
│ argument with a default if hasattr(greeting, 'kwdefaults') and     │
│ greeting.kwdefaults: # If 'greeting' is a keyword-only argument    │
│ with a default, allow overrides if len(greeting) > 1: # If another │
│ keyword argument is provided, it's an override return              │
│ f'{greeting[0]} world' return f'{greeting} world' [/patched]       │
